<Base>
  <h1>weir — a typed shell</h1>
  <p>
    A typed shell scripting language inspired by F#. Shell commands and
    typed expressions share one syntax, and the whole file typechecks —
    PATH lookups included — before anything runs: a broken script fails
    up front instead of halfway through its side effects.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://weir.sh/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
  <p>
    Windows: <code>irm https://weir.sh/install.ps1 | iex</code> — one
    static binary, no runtime. The script is generated per release with
    that release's checksums baked in;
    <a href="/docs/install/">docs/INSTALL</a> has the details.
  </p>

